# The app's security headers ride on every page and file the app
# serves (issue #70). The policy names the app's own origin — its
# own script, styles and icons, its own API and socket, framed by
# nobody — and one guest: the shared feedback service stands in
# connect-src, because the Feedback page's form posts to it
# (issue #20). It stands in this one rule rather than the page's
# own because Pages merges a page rule's policy with this one
# instead of replacing it, and two policies are enforced as
# their intersection. The self-host server sends the same
# headers from its own code; the two lists are kept alike by
# hand.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://feedback.certifiable.media; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
# The app files must never ride a stale cache. A browser holding an
# old app.js against a newer API shape stalls on load, so these files
# revalidate on every load; unchanged files still answer 304.
/boot.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
# The installable-app files follow the same rule: the manifest, the
# worker script and the icons revalidate rather than sit in a cache,
# so a new release is what every open gets. The manifest also names
# its own content type, the one browsers ask for by name.
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/icons/icon-192.png
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/icons/icon-512.png
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/icons/icon-maskable-512.png
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/icons/icon-180.png
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/icons/icon-64.png
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/icons/icon.svg
  Cache-Control: no-cache
# The wordmark's font follows the same rule, so a new cut of it
# is what every open gets.
/fonts/comfortaa-bold.woff2
  Cache-Control: no-cache
# The public pages (issue #14) follow the same rule: the front
# page's script and the standalone Terms, Help and Feedback
# pages revalidate on every load, so a change to the words is
# what every open gets. Each page is named in both its forms —
# the .html path and the pretty path — because the rules match
# the final address after the redirect.
/feedback.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/terms
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/terms.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/help
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/help.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/help/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/feedback
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/feedback.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
